    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18897" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀψόρροος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀψίνθ-ρρους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄψ, ῥέω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>back-flowing,
			refluent,</i> Homeric epith. of Ocean, regarded as a stream
				<i>encircling</i> the earth and <i>flowing back</i> into
			itself, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				18.399
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.65
			</span></i>.</div>
